  "body": "#560 and #551 are merged into upstream main; this branch merges upstream/main. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- **Electrode as a tool** (`ToolKind::Electrode`, `crates/tools/src/electrode.rs`). It reuses the existing `Tool` fields: `diameter` = face X, `width` = face Y, `flute_len` = length below the holder, `shank_len` = pickup offset. rpm 0 and a sharp face are required by law. A garbled electrode is refused by name at AddTool / ChangeTool / the library reader. `EDM-E10X6` joins the starter catalog, and the project file round-trips the kind.\n- **Sinker Burn op** (`OpType::SinkerBurn`, tag 41, `Section::Sinker`, `Family::Sinker`). It is admitted only on a `sinker_edm` machine; on any other machine the family door refuses it by name. Milling ops on a sinker stay refused (#530). Only an electrode mounts it.\n- **Depth from a stated datum.** The datum is the work top, the cavity floor (a stand-off) or the electrode tip at the approach plane. A burn past the cavity floor datum, past the model's floor, or deeper than the electrode is long is refused by name (`crates/motion/src/sinker.rs`).\n- **Spark gap** (coordinator note from #560's review). The op names a condition id, which is required. The command checks that the setup's machine is a sinker EDM, then asks `Edm::condition` for `ConditionField::Gap` only, never a wire field. Lookup is by id only, never by role. The tip stops one gap above the floor. The op's stamp digests the resolved gap, so a re-stated condition marks the op stale.\n- **CL**: an approach rapid, one feed plunge and a rapid retract. Golden: `crates/app/tests/golden/sinker_burn_cavity.cl`.\n- **Stock-sim verification** (#290 D7). A new column-engine **box atom** (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/dexel_box.rs`, `simulate_box`) sweeps the face grown by the gap and is exact per column. The program verdict (`simulate_document`, carry walk) cuts sinker ops with it. The field eye (stock view and playback) refuses an electrode program by name; it has no box atom yet. Rest masks count an electrode as removing nothing, which is the safe side.\n- **UI**: a minimal Sinker Burn op page (`sinker_page.rs`) keeps the tab law and edits through `EditOperationParams`. The full sinker pages are #548. The tool editor gains an electrode X/Y row.\n- **MCP**: no new tool is needed. `add_tool` (definition), `add_operation` (kind \"Sinker Burn\"), `edit_operation`, `generate` and `undo` drive the same undoable commands, and a test pins this.\n- **Posting**: refused. #542 owns the sinker post (#533 the wire). `post_serves` is only the picker's listing law, so the post door itself refuses: `posting_family::edm_at_post`, called by every writer (`post_setup`/`post_script` via `post_script_body`, the per-mount `post_each` and the per-op writer) right after `op_streams`, refuses any program whose setup's machine is a wire or sinker EDM by name (\"Setup1: no post for a sinker EDM machine yet (#542) - Burn0 is not posted and no file is written; ...\") before a byte is written. The MCP `post` tool and the script `post` verb ride the same writers. Pinned by `sinker_burn_held::the_post_refuses_a_burn_on_its_sinker_until_an_edm_dialect_ships` and the MCP leg of `sinker_burn::the_sinker_burn_is_driven_over_mcp_with_the_gui_commands`.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/541-sinker-burn-depth.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning tests in `crates/app/tests/sinker_burn.rs`:\n  - `sinker_burn_cavity_matches_golden`\n  - `a_rectangular_electrode_burns_its_cavity_to_the_stated_depth`: the column tops sit at the floor inside the face plus gap and are untouched outside it, and the program verdict reads 0 gouge cells.\n  - `a_burn_deeper_than_the_cavity_is_convicted_by_the_stock_sim`: a 1 mm overburn is convicted.\n  - `a_depth_past_the_floor_datum_is_refused_by_name`: all three datums.\n  - `a_sinker_burn_needs_a_sinker_and_a_stated_condition`\n  - `an_electrode_is_refused_at_add_tool_when_garbled_and_round_trips_the_file`\n  - `the_sinker_burn_is_driven_over_mcp_with_the_gui_commands` (ends with the MCP `post` tool refused by name, no file written)\n  - `a_spark_gap_that_lifts_the_tip_out_of_the_work_is_refused_by_name`: a gap placing the tip at or above the approach plane, or not smaller than the burn below the work top, is refused (review of #1131).\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_burn_held.rs::the_post_refuses_a_burn_on_its_sinker_until_an_edm_dialect_ships`: `post_setup`, `post_mounts` and `post_per_op` all refuse by name and the folder stays empty.\n- UI: the electrode tool glyph (`assets/ui/svg/tool-electrode.svg`, original, rasterised by `cargo xtask icons`) is pinned by `op_icon_table::every_tool_kind_has_its_own_svg_mastered_icon`.\n- Unit tests: `motion::sinker` (datums, refusals) and `tools::electrode`.\n- Registry and law tests were updated for the appended kind: `stamp_follows_every_input` (42 rows), `ribbon`, `tool_law`, the catalog order, and the UI tips and tab law.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base HEAD`) is green: tools, sim, motion, app and ui suites (10.5 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control** (#290 D10). The condition and the part are synthetic fixtures.\n- The field-arm stock view and playback of a sinker program are refused by name; that box atom is for #548.\n- No post: refused by name at the post door until #542 (sinker) / #533 (wire) ship a dialect. No orbit (#544), no undersize passes (#543).\n- Shared tables (op kinds, sections, families) take small appended edits. The wire stack (#532) will append next to them, so whichever PR merges second renumbers its kind tag.\n\nChangelog: Sinker EDM Sinker Burn: a rectangular electrode (a tool-library kind) burns to a depth read from the work top, cavity floor or electrode tip, placed by the machine condition's spark gap; a depth past the floor is refused by name and the stock sim convicts an overburn (#541)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #541\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
